    <section class="page is-active" id="page-home" data-page="home" aria-labelledby="home-title">
      <div class="shell home-hero">
        <div class="home-copy">
          <div class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> INDEPENDENT ENGINE DEVELOPMENT <span class="eyebrow-counter">/ 2026</span></div>
          <h1 id="home-title">BUILD<br>BEYOND<br><em>THE ORDINARY.</em></h1>
          <p class="hero-desc">A growing engine project exploring modern graphics, efficient runtimes and the tools behind interactive worlds. Developed openly. Tested deliberately.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-bright" href="#playground" data-tab-link="playground">Launch the playground <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button button-outline" href="#technology" data-tab-link="technology">Explore the technology <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
          <div class="hero-metadata"><div><b>01</b><small>C++20 CORE</small></div><div><b>02</b><small>WEB EXPERIMENTS</small></div><div><b>03</b><small>OPEN ROADMAP</small></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-visual" aria-label="Illustrated Xelqora engine concept artwork">
          <div class="visual-top"><span><span class="tiny-led"></span> XELQORA / VISUAL RESEARCH</span><span>PREVIEW 001</span></div>
          <div class="art-perspective"><div class="art-grid"></div><div class="orbital orbital-1"></div><div class="orbital orbital-2"></div><div class="orbital orbital-3"></div><div class="core-shape"><div class="core-inner"></div></div><div class="halo"></div></div>
          <div class="visual-bottom"><div><small>RENDER SYSTEM</small><b>EXPLORE NEW DIMENSIONS</b></div><div class="index-bars"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></div></div>
          <span class="visual-watermark">X / 01</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="shell"><div class="section-divider"></div><div class="section-intro intro-tight"><div><div class="eyebrow">THE PROJECT AT A GLANCE</div><h2>One foundation.<br><span class="subtle">More possibilities.</span></h2></div><p>From a tested headless core to experimental browser visuals, Xelqora is being built one component at a time. Explore what works today and what comes next.</p></div><div class="feature-grid three">
        <a href="#playground" data-tab-link="playground" class="feature-tile tile-visual"><div class="tile-meta">01 / INTERACTIVE</div><div class="tile-icon">◈</div><h3>Graphics playground</h3><p>Try procedural lighting, reflections and visual controls in your browser.</p><div class="tile-link">Open lab <span>↗</span></div></a>
        <a href="#technology" data-tab-link="technology" class="feature-tile"><div class="tile-meta">02 / FOUNDATION</div><div class="tile-icon">⌘</div><h3>Core architecture</h3><p>C++20 maths, timing, fixed-step scheduling and application lifecycle.</p><div class="tile-link">Explore core <span>↗</span></div></a>
        <a href="#roadmap" data-tab-link="roadmap" class="feature-tile"><div class="tile-meta">03 / FORWARD</div><div class="tile-icon">◎</div><h3>Built in the open</h3><p>Follow upcoming development milestones, priorities and technical decisions.</p><div class="tile-link">View roadmap <span>↗</span></div></a>
      </div></div>
      <div class="shell home-callout"><div><span class="eyebrow">OPEN BY DESIGN. POWERFUL BY NATURE.</span><h2>Curiosity is our starting point.<br><span class="subtle">Engineering is how we move forward.</span></h2></div><a class="button button-outline" href="#about" data-tab-link="about">Meet the project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    </section>
    <section class="page" id="page-playground" data-page="playground" aria-labelledby="playground-title" hidden>
      <div class="shell page-head"><div class="eyebrow">XELQORA / INTERACTIVE LABS</div><div class="page-headline"><h1 id="playground-title">SEE THE<br><em>ENGINE THINK.</em></h1><p>Run interactive experiments straight from the website. These demos use browser JavaScript and WebGL2; they do not execute the native C++ <?= $versionLabel ?> binary.</p></div></div>
      <div class="shell"><div class="subtabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Playground demonstrations"><button class="subtab active" type="button" data-lab="graphics" role="tab" aria-selected="true">01 / Rendering lab</button><button class="subtab" type="button" data-lab="physics" role="tab" aria-selected="false">02 / Physics lab</button><button class="subtab" type="button" data-lab="diagnostics" role="tab" aria-selected="false">03 / Diagnostics</button></div>
        <div class="lab-panel is-active" data-lab-panel="graphics"><div class="lab-main-grid"><div class="lab-render-frame"><div class="lab-topline"><span><span class="tiny-led"></span> LIVE WEBGL2 / PROCEDURAL RAY MARCHING</span><span id="render-fps">— FPS</span></div><div class="render-viewport" id="render-viewport"><canvas id="render-canvas" aria-label="Interactive procedural 3D rendering comparison"></canvas><div class="render-loading" id="render-loading">Initialising GPU demonstration…</div><div class="render-label left">ENHANCED LIGHTING</div><div class="render-label right">BASIC LIGHTING</div><div class="render-centerline" id="render-centerline"><span>↔</span></div></div><div class="lab-bottom"><span id="render-resolution">WEBGL2 / READY</span><span>DRAG TO ORBIT • SLIDE TO COMPARE</span></div></div><aside class="lab-controls"><div class="eyebrow">GRAPHICS PIPELINE</div><h2>Lighting.<br>Reimagined.</h2><p>Compare procedural ray-marched lighting with a simplified view. The enhanced mode uses additional shadow and reflection rays inside a fragment shader.</p><div class="control"><div class="control-head"><label for="comparison">Lighting comparison</label><output id="comparison-value">50 / 50</output></div><input type="range" id="comparison" min="0" max="100" value="50"></div><div class="control"><label for="scene-select">Environment</label><select id="scene-select"><option value="0">Studio / Chrome</option><option value="1">Aurora / Night</option><option value="2">Monolith / Ambient</option></select></div><div class="control"><label for="quality-select">Render scale</label><select id="quality-select"><option value="0.5">FSR 2.0x (50%)</option><option value="0.59">FSR 1.7x (59%)</option><option value="0.67">FSR 1.5x (67%)</option><option value="0.77">FSR 1.3x (77%)</option><option value="0.85" selected>Balanced (85%)</option><option value="1">Native (100%)</option></select></div><div class="control"><label for="upscaler-select">Upscaler</label><select id="upscaler-select"><option value="bilinear">Bilinear (no upscaler)</option><option value="fsr" selected>AMD FSR 1.0 (EASU + RCAS)</option></select></div><div class="control"><div class="control-head"><label for="sharpness">FSR sharpness</label><output id="sharpness-value" for="sharpness">0.50 stops</output></div><input type="range" id="sharpness" min="0" max="100" value="75"></div><div class="control-actions"><button class="button button-outline button-small" id="render-pause" type="button">Pause</button><button class="button button-outline button-small" id="render-reset" type="button">Reset camera</button></div><div class="minor-note"><b>Research demo, not product benchmark.</b> Shader calculations run on the visitor's GPU through WebGL2. Performance varies by browser and hardware; hardware RTX acceleration is not claimed. AMD FSR 1.0 (spatial upscaling) is a WebGL2 port of AMD's MIT-licensed FidelityFX source and runs only in this browser lab; the native C++ core has no renderer. This site is not affiliated with or endorsed by AMD. See <a href="assets/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt">third-party notices</a>.</div></aside></div></div>
        <div class="lab-panel" data-lab-panel="physics" hidden><div class="lab-main-grid"><div class="lab-render-frame"><div class="lab-topline"><span><span class="tiny-led"></span> LIVE 2D PHYSICS / JAVASCRIPT</span><span id="physics-fps">— FPS</span></div><div class="physics-viewport"><canvas id="physics-canvas" aria-label="Interactive bouncing ball physics simulation"></canvas><div class="physics-hint">Click or tap to spawn a ball. Drag an existing ball to throw it.</div></div><div class="lab-bottom"><span id="physics-count">0 OBJECTS</span><span>FIXED TIMESTEP / 120 HZ</span></div></div><aside class="lab-controls"><div class="eyebrow">MOTION EXPERIMENT</div><h2>Make<br>things move.</h2><p>A browser-only physics study with gravity, collisions, drag and an accumulator-based fixed timestep.</p><div class="control"><div class="control-head"><label for="gravity">Gravity</label><output id="gravity-value">720</output></div><input id="gravity" type="range" min="0" max="1600" step="20" value="720"></div><div class="control"><div class="control-head"><label for="bounce">Restitution</label><output id="bounce-value">0.80</output></div><input id="bounce" type="range" min="20" max="100" value="80"></div><div class="control-actions"><button class="button button-bright button-small" id="physics-add" type="button">Add object</button><button class="button button-outline button-small" id="physics-clear" type="button">Reset scene</button></div><div class="minor-note"><b>Separate prototype.</b> This simulator is written in JavaScript and does not prove a native Xelqora physics engine exists yet.</div></aside></div></div>
        <div class="lab-panel" data-lab-panel="diagnostics" hidden><div class="diagnostics-layout"><div><div class="eyebrow">ENVIRONMENT INSPECTOR</div><h2>Know your<br>runtime.</h2><p>Inspect the current browser's feature support and run a local deterministic scheduler check. This checks the browser lab, not the native C++ source.</p><button class="button button-bright" id="diag-run" type="button">Run browser checks <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button><div class="minor-note">The project-manifest check uses the optional PHP endpoint when available and falls back to data/project.json on static hosts such as GitHub Pages.</div></div><div class="diag-box"><div class="diag-top">XELQORA / DIAGNOSTICS <span id="diag-time">NOT RUN</span></div><div id="diag-results" aria-live="polite"><div class="diag-placeholder">Run checks to see results.</div></div></div></div></div>
        <div class="footnote-strip"><b>Why browser demos?</b> The native Xelqora <?= $versionLabel ?> is a headless C++ foundation. A future WebAssembly port could expose real core code to this playground; current labs are independent web prototypes.</div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="page" id="page-technology" data-page="technology" aria-labelledby="tech-title" hidden><div class="shell page-head"><div class="eyebrow">XELQORA / ENGINE SYSTEMS</div><div class="page-headline"><h1 id="tech-title">DESIGNED FOR<br><em>WHAT'S NEXT.</em></h1><p>Modular ambitions, measured progress. These are the foundations under development—not a list of completed production features.</p></div></div><div class="shell tech-layout"><div class="tech-feature"><span class="tech-number">01 — CORE</span><div class="tech-graphic"><div class="tech-graphic-inner">X<span> / </span>C++20</div><div class="tech-graphic-lines"></div></div><h2>Start with a reliable foundation.</h2><p><?= $versionLabel ?> explores lifecycle management, vector and matrix maths, fixed timestep scheduling and portable CMake builds. Its prototype has previously passed GCC and Clang test cases in a development environment; native Windows verification remains pending.</p><a href="https://github.com/MrNT10/Xelqora-engine" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link">Explore repository <span>↗</span></a></div><div class="tech-list"><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Rendering systems <small>RESEARCH</small></h3><p>WebGL2 procedural demos today; future renderer abstractions, scene materials, ray effects and cross-platform backends are goals.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Physics and simulation <small>EXPERIMENTAL</small></h3><p>Browser physics experiments explore collision behaviour and fixed-step timing. Native integration is not complete.</p></div></article><article><span>04</span><div><h3>Super resolution <small>PLANNED</small></h3><p>Xelqora Super Resolution (XSR) is a research direction. The browser rendering lab includes a WebGL2 port of AMD FSR 1.0 (spatial EASU + RCAS); FSR 2/3, frame generation and neural upscalers are not included.</p></div></article><article><span>05</span><div><h3>Audio and assets <small>PLANNED</small></h3><p>Future work includes audio playback, asset loading, error handling and packaging workflows.</p></div></article><article><span>06</span><div><h3>Release engineering <small>IN PROGRESS</small></h3><p>Automated tests, cross-platform builds, transparent release notes and an eventual stability-focused LTS channel.</p></div></article></div></div></section>
    <section class="page" id="page-roadmap" data-page="roadmap" aria-labelledby="roadmap-title" hidden><div class="shell page-head"><div class="eyebrow">XELQORA / DEVELOPMENT TRACKER</div><div class="page-headline"><h1 id="roadmap-title">THE ROAD<br><em>AHEAD.</em></h1><p>Progress is tracked by implementation and verification—not marketing dates. Features below may change as the engine matures.</p></div></div><div class="shell"><div class="roadmap-board" id="roadmap-board"><article class="roadmap-row"><div class="roadmap-step">01</div><div><h3>Core foundation</h3><p>Math, scheduling, application lifecycle</p></div><span class="roadmap-state">PROTOTYPE</span></article><article class="roadmap-row"><div class="roadmap-step">02</div><div><h3>Platform backend</h3><p>Windows event processing, input, windows</p></div><span class="roadmap-state">NEXT</span></article><article class="roadmap-row"><div class="roadmap-step">03</div><div><h3>Rendering interface</h3><p>RHI design, shader and projection conventions</p></div><span class="roadmap-state">RESEARCH</span></article><article class="roadmap-row"><div class="roadmap-step">04</div><div><h3>Asset and scene management</h3><p>Loading, scene graph and content flow</p></div><span class="roadmap-state">PLANNED</span></article><article class="roadmap-row"><div class="roadmap-step">05</div><div><h3>LTS distribution</h3><p>Stability criteria, release maintenance</p></div><span class="roadmap-state">PLANNED</span></article></div><div class="roadmap-foot"><b>Release philosophy</b><p>Core development is experimental. Stable and LTS releases will only be announced once real binaries, tests and maintenance expectations exist.</p></div></div></section>
    <section class="page" id="page-downloads" data-page="downloads" aria-labelledby="downloads-title" hidden><div class="shell page-head"><div class="eyebrow">XELQORA / DISTRIBUTION</div><div class="page-headline"><h1 id="downloads-title">GET THE<br><em>SOURCE.</em></h1><p>Source, experiments and release planning—all in one place. We only show working, verifiable links, not fictional binaries.</p></div></div><div class="shell downloads-grid"><article class="download-panel featured"><span class="download-type">SOURCE / GITHUB</span><div class="download-symbol">⌘</div><h2>Xelqora Engine</h2><p>Visit the project's public repository to inspect code, documentation and any releases actually published.</p><a class="button button-bright" href="https://github.com/MrNT10/Xelqora-engine" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article><article class="download-panel"><span class="download-type">EARLY-STAGE / EXPERIMENTAL</span><div class="availability">NOT VERIFIED FOR RELEASE</div><h2><?= $versionLabel ?> build</h2><p>A native C++20 headless foundation exists in reviewed source. The site does not claim a downloadable installer or complete game editor.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/MrNT10/Xelqora-engine/releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check actual GitHub releases <span>↗</span></a></article><article class="download-panel"><span class="download-type">STABILITY CHANNEL / PROPOSED</span><div class="availability">FUTURE CHANNEL</div><h2>Xelqora LTS</h2><p>A proposed long-term stability channel. No downloadable LTS release, support guarantee or Patreon entitlement is advertised here yet.</p><a class="text-link" href="#roadmap" data-tab-link="roadmap">See the release roadmap <span>→</span></a></article></div><div class="shell licence-strip"><b>Licence and attribution</b><p>Licence selection is being reviewed. Consult the applicable <code>LICENSE</code> file for each version in the GitHub repository. Previous GPL-covered releases keep their original terms; this site does not relicense code.</p></div></section>
    <section class="page" id="page-about" data-page="about" aria-labelledby="about-title" hidden><div class="shell page-head"><div class="eyebrow">XELQORA / OUR APPROACH</div><div class="page-headline"><h1 id="about-title">ENGINEERED<br><em>WITH INTENT.</em></h1><p>A focused independent development project, directed by MrNT10 and assisted by AI tools for design, implementation and code review.</p></div></div><div class="shell about-grid"><div class="about-statement"><span class="eyebrow">OPEN BY DESIGN. POWERFUL BY NATURE.</span><h2>Make room for experimentation.<br><span class="subtle">Back it with careful engineering.</span></h2><p>Xelqora is an evolving family of engine prototypes and technical research. Our focus is dependable foundations, clear documentation, independent reviews and honest feature claims.</p><div class="about-action"><a class="button button-bright" href="https://github.com/MrNT10/Xelqora-engine" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit MrNT10 on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><div class="about-facts"><div><span>PROJECT</span><b>Xelqora Engine</b></div><div><span>MAINTAINER</span><b>MrNT10</b></div><div><span>STATUS</span><b>Early-stage development</b></div><div><span>TOOLS</span><b>C++20, CMake, JavaScript, WebGL2, PHP</b></div><div><span>CONTRIBUTIONS</span><b>Human-directed, AI-assisted</b></div></div></div><div class="shell contact-panel"><div><div class="eyebrow">CONNECT</div><h2>Follow the build.</h2><p>Development updates, source code and eventual validated releases will be linked from the project repository.</p></div><a class="button button-outline" href="https://github.com/MrNT10/Xelqora-engine" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub repository ↗</a></div></section>
